{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "PSA",
  "chapter": 44,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "To the chief Musician for the sons of Korah, Maschil. We have heard with our ears, O God, our fathers have told us, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "what",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " work thou didst in their days, in the times of old.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "How",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou didst drive out the heathen with thy hand, and didst plant them; ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "how",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thou didst afflict the people, and cast them out.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For they obtained not the land in possession by their own sword, neither did their own arm save them: but thy right hand, and thy arm, and the light of thy countenance, because thou hadst a favor to them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou art my King, O God: command deliverances for Jacob.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Through thee will we push down our enemies: through thy name we will tread them under that rise up against us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For I will not trust in my bow, neither shall my sword save me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou hast saved us from our enemies, and hast put them to shame that hated us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In God we boast all the day long, and praise thy name for ever. Selah.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But thou hast cast off, and put us to shame; and goest not forth with our armies.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us to turn back from the enemy: and they who hate us plunder for themselves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou hast given us like sheep ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "appointed",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for food; and hast scattered us among the heathen.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou sellest thy people for naught, and dost not increase ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "thy wealth",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by their price.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us a reproach to our neighbors, a scorn and a derision to them that are around us.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou makest us a by-word among the heathen, a shaking of the head among the people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My confusion ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " continually before me, and the shame of my face hath covered me,",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For the voice of him that reproacheth and blasphemeth; by reason of the enemy and avenger.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "All this is come upon us; yet we have not forgotten thee, neither have we dealt falsely in thy covenant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Our heart is not turned back, neither have our steps declined from thy way;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though thou hast severely broke us in the place of dragons, and covered us with the shades of death.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If we have forgotten the name of our God, or stretched out our hands to a strange god;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Will not God search out this? for he knoweth the secrets of the heart.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, for thy sake are we killed all the day long; we are counted as sheep for the slaughter.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Awake, why sleepest thou, O LORD? arise, cast ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "us",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " not off for ever.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Why hidest thou thy face, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " forgettest our affliction and our oppression?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For our soul is bowed down to the dust: our belly cleaveth to the earth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "PSA.44.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:PSA.44.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Arise for our help, and redeem us for thy mercies' sake.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
